  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures a Mountain Goats performance at the Knitting Factory on October 8, 2004 [1]. The setlist includes sixteen songs, starting with \"This Year\" and \"Short Song About the 10 Freeway\" [1]. Other tracks in the sequence are \"Southwood Plantation Road,\" \"Linda Blair was Born Innocent,\" and \"Your Belgian Things\" [1]. The middle portion features \"Slow West Vultures,\" \"Tollund Man,\" and \"I Will Survive\" [1]. Later songs include \"Tallahassee,\" \"Dance Music,\" and \"Lion's Teeth\" [1]. The set concludes with \"First Few Desperate Hours,\" \"Commandante,\" \"Jenny,\" \"See America Right,\" and \"Palmcorder Yajna\" [1]. The uploader notes that technical difficulties plagued the set [1]. Despite these issues, the band performed \"Commandante\" [1]. An encore was missing from this recording [1]. The missing encore songs were \"Shadow Song\" and \"Orange by Furniture Huschle\" [1]. This is the only available recording of this specific show [1]. It is the sixty-first show in the archive's collection for the band [2]. The previous archived show was on October 4, 2004, at The Magic Stick [2]. The recording runs for sixty-three minutes [1]. \"Short Song About the 10 Freeway\" is a rare track with five archived performances [2]. \"I Will Survive\" and \"Lion's Teeth\" are first in the archive [2].",
